  "body": "When there should be outbound federation traffic:\r\n\r\n```\r\n2022-10-21 23:33:28,436 - synapse.metrics.background_process_metrics - 244 - ERROR - process_event_queue_for_federation-6 - Background process 'process_event_queue_for_federation' threw an exception\r\n...\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/home/synapse/src/synapse/synapse/metrics/background_process_metrics.py\", line 240, in run\r\n    return await func(*args, **kwargs)\r\n  File \"/home/synapse/src/synapse/synapse/federation/sender/__init__.py\", line 539, in _process_event_queue_loop\r\n    last_id = next(reversed(event_ids))\r\nTypeError: 'dict_keys' object is not reversible\r\n```\r\n\r\nTurns out that `dict.keys` is, as the error says, not reversible on Python 3.7.\r\n\r\nI think this was introduced by #13813 (and I think it was my rubbish suggestion). ",
